    {"text": "Reading fiction before bed is far more relaxing than watching television.", "intent": "statement", "domain": "everyday", "tags": ["books", "wellness"]},
    {"text": "The best debugging tool is still a well-placed print statement.", "intent": "statement", "domain": "technical", "tags": ["programming", "humor"]},
    {"text": "Nothing beats the smell of fresh bread baking in the oven on a Sunday morning.", "intent": "statement", "domain": "everyday", "tags": ["cooking"]},
    # -- extra medium security --
    {"text": "I am setting up a home network and I want to make sure my WiFi is secure. I have changed the default router password but I am not sure what else I should do. What are the essential security settings I should configure on a home wireless router?", "intent": "question", "domain": "security", "tags": ["wifi", "home-network"]},
    {"text": "My teenager wants to start using social media and I am concerned about privacy and safety. What settings and practices should we put in place to protect their personal information while still letting them participate in online communities with their friends?", "intent": "question", "domain": "security", "tags": ["privacy", "parenting"]},
    {"text": "I keep hearing about data breaches affecting companies I have accounts with. Is there a practical way to find out if my personal information has been exposed, and what steps should I take if it has been compromised in a breach?", "intent": "question", "domain": "security", "tags": ["data-breach", "privacy"]},
    # -- extra medium formal --
    {"text": "As project lead, I need to communicate a two-week delay in our product launch to external stakeholders. The delay is due to unexpected integration issues with a third-party vendor. How should I frame this communication to maintain trust while being transparent about the situation?", "intent": "question", "domain": "formal", "tags": ["communication", "project-management"]},
    {"text": "I have been asked to moderate a panel discussion at an industry conference on the future of remote work. The panelists have very different viewpoints. Can you suggest some thought-provoking questions that would generate a substantive discussion without becoming confrontational?", "intent": "request", "domain": "formal", "tags": ["events", "professional"]},
    # -- extra medium informal --
    {"text": "My friends and I are starting a book club but we are all terrible at finishing books on time. Any creative ideas for keeping everyone motivated and actually reading, without it feeling like homework?", "intent": "question", "domain": "informal", "tags": ["books", "social"]},
    {"text": "I just moved into my first apartment and my cooking repertoire consists entirely of scrambled eggs and frozen pizza. Give me five actually easy meals that a complete kitchen novice can make without screwing up too badly.", "intent": "request", "domain": "informal", "tags": ["cooking"]},
    # -- extra long statements --
    {"text": "One thing I have noticed after mentoring junior developers for several years is that the biggest predictor of success is not technical skill or even intelligence but rather the willingness to ask questions and admit when you do not understand something. The juniors who struggle the most are often the ones who nod along in meetings pretending everything makes sense, then go back to their desks and spend hours stuck on something that a five-minute conversation could have resolved. The best thing a senior developer can do is create an environment where asking questions is not just tolerated but actively encouraged and rewarded.", "intent": "statement", "domain": "technical", "tags": ["mentoring", "career"]},
    {"text": "Travel has taught me that the most memorable experiences rarely come from checking items off a tourist bucket list. Some of my best travel memories are mundane moments: getting lost in a neighborhood in Lisbon and stumbling into a tiny family-owned restaurant where nobody spoke English, sitting in a park in Kyoto watching an elderly couple practice tai chi in the morning mist, or sharing a meal with a local family in rural Peru who insisted on feeding me despite having very little themselves. These unplanned encounters gave me a deeper understanding of different cultures than any guided tour ever could.", "intent": "statement", "domain": "everyday", "tags": ["travel", "reflection"]},
    # -- extra security long --
    {"text": "Our small startup just landed its first enterprise client and they have sent us a security questionnaire with over two hundred questions covering everything from data encryption practices to employee background checks to disaster recovery plans. We are a team of eight people and our infrastructure is entirely on AWS. We use standard security practices but we have never had to formalize them into policies or documentation. I need to respond to this questionnaire within two weeks. Can you help me prioritize which areas to address first and suggest practical shortcuts for a small team to demonstrate a strong security posture without having a dedicated security department?", "intent": "request", "domain": "security", "tags": ["compliance", "startup"]},
    # -- extra long multi_turn --
    {"text": "Coming back to the conversation we had about optimizing my e-commerce website for performance. You suggested implementing lazy loading for images, using a CDN for static assets, and adding Redis caching for frequently accessed product data. I have implemented all three suggestions and the page load time improved from four point two seconds to one point eight seconds, which is great. However, I am now seeing occasional stale data issues where product prices update in the database but the cached version shows the old price for several minutes. How should I implement a cache invalidation strategy that keeps the performance benefits while ensuring data consistency?", "intent": "multi_turn", "domain": "technical", "tags": ["web", "performance", "caching"]},
    # -- extra formal long --
    {"text": "I am a department head at a mid-sized university and I have been tasked with writing a strategic plan for expanding our online course offerings over the next five years. The plan needs to address faculty training and incentives for developing online content, technology infrastructure requirements, student support services for remote learners, quality assurance mechanisms to ensure online courses meet the same standards as in-person instruction, and a realistic budget projection. This will be presented to the provost and the board of trustees. Can you help me create an outline that covers all of these areas and suggests specific metrics we should use to measure success?", "intent": "request", "domain": "formal", "tags": ["education", "strategy", "planning"]},
    # -- extra everyday questions to reach targets --
    {"text": "I have noticed my houseplants keep getting brown tips on their leaves even though I water them on a regular schedule. Could this be related to the water quality or humidity in my apartment?", "intent": "question", "domain": "everyday", "tags": ["gardening", "household"]},
    {"text": "What are some underrated European cities worth visiting that most tourists overlook in favor of the usual destinations like Paris and Rome?", "intent": "question", "domain": "everyday", "tags": ["travel"]},
    {"text": "I want to reduce my household waste but going completely zero-waste feels impossible with a busy family. What are realistic first steps?", "intent": "question", "domain": "everyday", "tags": ["environment", "lifestyle"]},
    {"text": "My car makes a strange clicking noise when I turn the steering wheel to the left. Is this something dangerous or can it wait until my next scheduled maintenance?", "intent": "question", "domain": "everyday", "tags": ["cars"]},
    {"text": "I have trouble falling asleep because my mind races with thoughts about work. Are there any evidence-based techniques for quieting the mind before bed?", "intent": "question", "domain": "everyday", "tags": ["health", "wellness"]},
    {"text": "How do I choose a good bottle of wine for a dinner party if I know almost nothing about wine?", "intent": "question", "domain": "everyday", "tags": ["food", "social"]},
    {"text": "My elderly neighbor mentioned she needs help setting up video calls with her grandchildren. What is the simplest platform I could teach her to use?", "intent": "question", "domain": "everyday", "tags": ["technology", "elderly-care"]},
    # -- extra requests to reach targets --
